WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.390
Take two identical cylinders, side by side
in a room that stays at a steady temperature.

2
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:09.210
Each holds the same
amount of the same gas,

3
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:12.820
sealed by a piston, in
the same starting state.

4
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:16.160
In the first, the piston
creeps out slowly.

5
00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:19.030
In the second, it moves out suddenly.

6
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.450
Both end at the same volume.

7
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.030
Does one of them end up
colder than the other?

8
00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.090
If so, which one, and why?

9
00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:30.380
In this mission, you'll
meet four special processes,

10
00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.830
each keeping one thing fixed.

11
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.400
Then you'll read isotherms
on a pressure–volume diagram,

12
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:39.960
and see why the hotter ones
sit higher on the diagram.

13
00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:43.260
Your mission: predict
which gas ends up colder,

14
00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:44.510
and explain why.
